[Music]  hi i'm kevin konink i'm  from belgium  i work as an auditor at the european  court of auditors  having background as an author at  regional or local level i  i thought it was very interesting to  join the court because it's a relatively  small institution it deals with a lot of  policy areas whether it's agriculture  cohesion i felt like it would enable me  to to get a good understanding of the  whole  new project  [Music]  previously i was working in brussels  which is of course bigger but i have to  say that i was really surprised by  luxembourg it offers a lot of  opportunities it's smaller but it has  all the advantages that the capital has  i think the court offers excellent  training opportunities you're also  surrounded with a lot of knowledgeable  colleagues who are happy to share their  knowledge  [Music]  it's true that we spent quite a bit of  time in the office to prepare audits to  prepare reports to analyze documents  but we also go on the spot because we  feel it's important to see how projects  are being implemented and how the money  is being spent on the spot  [Music]  to be able to see how management and  control systems work in different member  states how the budget is being  implemented across the member states and  even outside the eu and to be able to  compare those systems and draw lessons  from one member state and maybe to apply  it in another  a small part of a much bigger chain but  in my role as an auditor i'm able to  contribute by auditing and communicating  the results of our audits so citizens  know how their money is being spent  [Applause]

